Z||000009||fierosound||05-08-2000||11:56 PM||||TooLow...<P>6x50 watts @ 4 ohms gets me 115-120db.  BUT extremely high SOUND QUALITY is what I also have.||||reg||10
Z||000010||fierosound||05-09-2000||12:03 AM||||Homicidal...<P>180 watts per sub (360 peak per sub) should be more than enough for anybody.  I'm only running 50 watts each!  More important, is the 93db sensitivity (efficiency) which means you can get more SPL with less power.  Check the specs on some other subs.  Those with a sensitivity of 86db (and lower) NEED LOTS of power to work properly!  <P>About your nickname... does it relate somehow to the amount of WATTS and BASS you think you need??   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Homicidal||05-09-2000||12:42 AM||||My 10" Polk Audio db has a 300W RMS and 600W peak.  I am pushing 125-250W on it. <P>50W each just sounds like it will give minor bass and nothing earth shattering.<P>I get all my mirrors in my cars to shake off one sub, and since it cost me.....$0 I am happy!||||reg||1
Z||000012||RiceCooker||05-09-2000||02:59 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierosound:<BR><B>If you use a monster 15" long, with a basket 8 inches deep, your box will have to be significantly deeper</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I really wish I had this problem<P>||||reg||10
Z||000013||Alex4mula||05-09-2000||03:42 PM||||Fierosound, Loki;<P>Are your seats covered with cloth or leather? I'm looking for that setup but I'm worried that the sub will not sound as good through my leather seats. If I install the subs there my seats will allways be all the way to the back (6' driver) and I'n not sure how the waves will travel with the seat back stuck to the grill. Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000014||fierosound||05-09-2000||07:28 PM||||I guess you picked the perfect moniker Homicidal      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>What kind of SPL does that generate??    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P><BR> <A HREF="http://www.polkmomo.com/mm100.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.polkmomo.com/mm100.html</A> <P>The above site give specs for the 10" MOMO (the Competition series) sub from Polk Audio.  It has a sensitivity rating of 85db.   I'm not sure which model you have.  <P>The rule of thumb in car audio is:  <P>To DOUBLE the volume, you need 10 TIMES the power.   That is why 50 watts does little for your sub, as it needs more power anyway.  This is where some people get in trouble...  they mismatch their speakers and amplifier power.  Mine could use more power but DOESN'T NEED IT.  If I put it into competition again, I might do something just to generate more SPL points.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000015||fierosound||05-09-2000||07:30 PM||||Alex...<P>Leave 1 inch between your seatback and grill.  If you can't, I suppose you need to look a for an alternate method of installing subs.  <P>Most trunk equipped cars fire their subs THROUGH the backseat without any problems.  The nature of the low frequency soundwaves is quite different from that of highs and is less prone to being blocked.  <P>No matter what, your bass will have to be better than a car that has no subs at all!<p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
